# temple_facade -- the Music Room's dress. Placed at temple.part's own origin and yaw, so these
# are its local coordinates: the striped cube from y 0.5 to 9.5 with its faces at +/-5.5, the
# peristyle's entablature ring at y 4.65, the parapet well open at y 10.0.
#
# Three things happen here. The ten painted bands become ten courses of real moulded stone, each
# a single stretched stripe_panel with a chamfer top and bottom so the course above throws a line
# on the one below and the stripes stop looking like a decal. The drum the dome used to sit on
# goes back on the roof. And the dome itself is on the ground in front of the porch, because
# island.txt says a hurricane took it and this is where it stopped.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the ten courses
# The shell already steps the cobalt bands 0.075 proud of the white ones; these panels sit on
# whichever face they belong to and stand 0.07 further out again, and are cut 0.07 over-wide so
# the four faces' panels overlap at the corners instead of leaving a notch.
piece models/own/arch/stripe_panel.obj       0.000  0.500  -5.500  11.140 1.000 1.000    0.0 0.0   0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.7
piece models/own/arch/stripe_panel.obj       0.000  0.500   5.500  11.140 1.000 1.000  180.0 0.0   0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.7
